WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.964 --> 00:00:06.486
The children heard the lovely sound of a low horn.

2
00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.186
"What's that?"

3
00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:08.467
asked Mandy.

4
00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:09.507
"It's the hunting horn.

5
00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:13.109
The hunt is about to begin!"

6
00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:13.409
Helene yelled.

7
00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:14.649
"Everyone goes hunting with the king.

8
00:00:30.592 --> 00:00:32.514
Everyone but the servants, of course."

9
00:00:34.635 --> 00:00:36.797
A man with a pack of dogs appeared.

10
00:00:38.098 --> 00:00:41.081
The dogs were barking and pulling at their leashes.

11
00:00:41.101 --> 00:00:42.962
"What are they hunting?"

12
00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.223
asked Vinnie.

13
00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:48.046
"Most likely fox," Helene said.

14
00:00:48.066 --> 00:00:51.369
Another horn rang out.

15
00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:53.731
They heard horses trotting.

16
00:00:53.751 --> 00:00:56.973
"Do they hunt every day?"

17
00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:58.354
asked Mandy.

18
00:00:58.374 --> 00:01:00.136
"Of course!"

19
00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:01.337
said Helene.

20
00:01:01.357 --> 00:01:03.899
"Hunting is the king's favorite sport.

21
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.421
Yesterday he got a deer."

22
00:01:08.263 --> 00:01:09.845
Mandy burned with anger.

23
00:01:10.886 --> 00:01:14.609
She whispered to Vinnie, "Hunting is not a sport!

24
00:01:15.109 --> 00:01:17.251
It's killing poor animals!"

25
00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:20.494
Helene took Mandy's hand.

26
00:01:20.514 --> 00:01:25.899
"Since the king is out hunting, I'll show you the palace," she said.

27
00:01:28.476 --> 00:01:30.938
The children all ran into the palace.

28
00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:35.382
"Ooh!" said Mandy.

29
00:01:35.402 --> 00:01:38.424
"Wow!" said Vinnie.

30
00:01:38.444 --> 00:01:42.587
"Shh!" said Helene.

31
00:01:42.607 --> 00:01:46.551
"If you want to see it all, you have to be quiet."

32
00:01:47.511 --> 00:01:49.593
Everything in the palace sparkled.

33
00:01:50.714 --> 00:01:53.816
Paintings of the king were on the walls and ceilings.

34
00:01:55.037 --> 00:01:57.900
The furniture was covered in gold and velvet.

35
00:02:00.024 --> 00:02:04.686
"There are about 700 rooms in Versailles," Helene explained.

36
00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:08.328
She stopped in front of huge double doors.

37
00:02:09.108 --> 00:02:10.409
Helene looked around.

38
00:02:11.509 --> 00:02:14.331
She wanted to make sure no one was watching.

39
00:02:14.351 --> 00:02:19.613
"And this room is the most beautiful of all!"

40
00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.034
cried Helene.

41
00:02:21.054 --> 00:02:22.854
"It's my favorite!"

42
00:02:23.835 --> 00:02:25.996
She opened the double doors wide.

43
00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.662
Vinnie and Mandy followed her inside.

44
00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:32.904
Their mouths dropped open.

45
00:02:33.985 --> 00:02:35.406
It was a large hall.

46
00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.073
There were 17 glass doors that looked out to the gardens.

47
00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.916
On the walls were large decorated mirrors.

48
00:02:46.936 --> 00:02:51.240
"This is the Hall of Mirrors.

49
00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:52.381
It has 357 mirrors!"

50
00:02:52.441 --> 00:02:52.821
said Helene.

51
00:02:56.684 --> 00:02:59.366
"King Louis meets very important people in here.

52
00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.608
I make believe this is my dancing room."

53
00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:05.830
Helene twirled across the floor.

54
00:03:06.891 --> 00:03:10.753
She did not see two guards with long spears enter the hall.

55
00:03:10.774 --> 00:03:12.515
"You children!"

56
00:03:13.135 --> 00:03:13.876
one shouted.

57
00:03:13.896 --> 00:03:16.397
"In the name of His Royal Highness, stop!"

58
00:03:17.078 --> 00:03:21.120
"Uh-oh!" Helene stopped dancing.

59
00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.301
"Follow me!"

60
00:03:23.762 --> 00:03:26.164
Helene led the children down a hallway.

61
00:03:27.184 --> 00:03:30.705
Along the walls, gold statues held up crystal lights.

62
00:03:30.725 --> 00:03:34.086
"Stop!" yelled the other guard.

63
00:03:34.606 --> 00:03:36.067
The guards ran after them.

64
00:03:36.087 --> 00:03:38.727
"What happens if they catch us?"

65
00:03:39.408 --> 00:03:40.028
asked Vinnie.

66
00:03:40.048 --> 00:03:42.889
"Don't worry," giggled Helene.

67
00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:46.630
"We can get away through the gardens.

68
00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.930
But we'll have to hide first!"

69
00:03:51.151 --> 00:03:53.732
Helene turned a corner and went into a room.

70
00:03:55.356 --> 00:03:57.998
Lace and ostrich feathers were everywhere.

71
00:03:58.878 --> 00:04:00.719
A group of women sat sewing.

72
00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.621
One woman saw the children.

73
00:04:03.641 --> 00:04:07.823
"Are the guards chasing you again, Helene?"

74
00:04:08.343 --> 00:04:09.164
she smiled.

75
00:04:10.284 --> 00:04:12.305
Helene blew the woman a kiss.

76
00:04:13.066 --> 00:04:15.607
Then she led the children out another door.

77
00:04:17.008 --> 00:04:19.149
Helene ducked into another room.

78
00:04:19.169 --> 00:04:22.631
"How does she know this place so well?"

79
00:04:23.271 --> 00:04:24.252
gasped Mandy.

80
00:04:24.956 --> 00:04:26.638
Vinnie hurried right behind.

81
00:04:27.238 --> 00:04:28.780
He wondered the same thing.

82
00:04:30.381 --> 00:04:34.144
Suddenly, he bumped into a woman, and her head rolled off.

83
00:04:35.466 --> 00:04:37.607
"Ahhh!" he screamed.
